ith snippet 'This is a sample transcript snippet that appears in the video at the cited moment.') is opened from the chat\",\n      \"when\": \"CitationModal renders for that citation\",\n      \"then\": \"the supplied snippet text is visible inside the modal alongside the video player: the player iframe (title 'YouTube video player') is still present in the same render, and the snippet text appears in the modal's scrollable content area below the player. This fails today — the component renders no snippet anywhere and CitationModal.test.tsx:35-41 pins that absence\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-2\",\n      \"given\": \"a YouTube citation whose snippet contains embedded newlines (e.g. 'line one\\\\nline two\\\\nline three', as Dynamous ingest builds with '{heading}\\\\n\\\\n{text}')\",\n      \"when\": \"CitationModal renders it\",\n      \"then\": \"the full multiline snippet is present as text content and its line breaks are preserved on screen — the element rendering the excerpt carries the codebase's verbatim-text idiom, observable as element.style.whiteSpace === 'pre-wrap'. Asserting only getByText(fullMultilineString) is insufficient: jsdom textContent retains \\\\n even when breaks visually collapse. This fails today because no snippet is rendered at all\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-3\",\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"given\": \"a citation with a valid YouTube video_url and start_seconds=754 (the existing mockCitation)\",\n      \"when\": \"CitationModal renders it\",\n      \"then\": \"playback and timestamp behavior is unchanged from today: the iframe src contains youtube.com/embed/dQw4w9WgXcQ?start=754&autoplay=1 and the 'Open on YouTube' link href contains watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ&t=754s (kept behaviour; the existing iframe-src and external-link tests keep passing unmodified in intent)\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-4\",\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"given\": \"an open citation modal\",\n      \"when\": \"the user presses Escape, clicks the close button, or clicks the backdrop\",\n      \"then\": \"onClose fires exactly once per interaction in all three paths as today, and body scroll is locked (overflow hidden) while mounted and restored on unmount (kept behaviour)\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AC-5\",\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"given\": \"a citation whose snippet is empty or whitespace-only (snippet: '' or '   ')\",\n      \"when\": \"CitationModal renders it\",\n      \"then\": \"no transcript section, heading or empty box appears, and the rest of the modal (player, timestamp range, external link) is unchanged from today (kept behaviour — holds on the unchanged tree because no snippet UI exists yet, and must still hold after the feature lands via the trim guard)\",\n      \"seam\": \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"Frontend-only change in CitationModal.tsx: no backend, API, type or state changes; Citation.snippet is already populated end-to-end (api.ts:53, rag/tools.py:211, repository.py snippet column) and needs no work.\",\n    \"No new external dependencies (the issue bans them); line-break preservation uses the existing CSS whiteSpace:'pre-wrap' idiom (Message.tsx:202), not <br/> splitting.\",\n    \"formatTimestamp keeps its exported signature — it is imported by Message.tsx.\",\n    \"Dynamous citations keep routing directly to lesson_url via ChatArea.handleCitationClick and never reach the modal.\",\n    \"Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit are untouched.\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.test.tsx is